1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
At three in the morning, a feed pump trips.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,500
The engineer needs an answer, but the lesson was never written.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:15,000
Across fifty-seven unplanned-failure records, fourteen appear in no lesson at all.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The Hub shows exactly where the plant's knowledge is missing.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Now the Engineer asks why GA-1201A tripped.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Every claim links back to evidence.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Open one citation and we land on the exact source,

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
with its revision and approval status.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
The trace then shows how the answer was produced and checked.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Next, the question changes: how do we get past the trip?

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The Hub stops it before any model is called and points to the permit route.

12
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,000
But when an approved bypass procedure already exists,

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The Hub returns it exactly as written, together with its permit conditions.

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Safe does not mean refusing everything.

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:32,000
The asset view connects typed tags, proof tests, and maintenance history.

16
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:37,000
The drawing's hotspots were transcribed by an agent,

17
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:42,000
so The Hub marks them pending review instead of passing them off as fact.

18
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Failure Memory then follows the misalignment chain to a cracked coupling element.

19
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:56,000
When we ask for a lesson on that task, The Hub abstains.

20
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:03,000
It shows the missing coverage, then ranks the next gap to address.

21
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:10,000
At the top of the queue is YD-2301.

22
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,000
From here, responsibility changes hands.

23
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:26,000
The Reviewing Supervisor requests and accepts a stored draft.

24
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The screen then switches to the Manager, the only role allowed to publish.

25
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Notice that the recount has not moved: publication has not happened yet.

26
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:51,000
The system can prepare the work, but it cannot cross the final human gate on its own.

27
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,000
The Hub knows what the plant is missing.
